$ enola plan --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola plan [flags] [path...] [repo_path|config_path]

The pre-edit contract: which declared constraints govern an intended change,
its blast radius over the current snapshot, the verdicts that would appear or
vanish if each path left every part (one re-evaluation over the loaded
snapshot), and, for a --patch, the constraint verdicts that WOULD appear,
evaluated over a scratch copy BEFORE any edit lands in the tree. The working tree and its snapshot are never
written; a report, never a gate.

Positional arguments naming an existing directory or a .yaml/.yml file pick
the repository or config (first match wins); every other positional is a
path target. Use --paths for a target that is itself a directory.

Exit codes:
  0  the report was produced (its verdicts are for the caller to weigh)
  2  the command could not run (bad patch, missing snapshot for --symbols,
     invalid declaration)

Flags:
  -json
    	emit the report as JSON instead of text
  -no-radius
    	skip the re-evaluation that names the verdicts a move of each path would change
  -patch string
    	a unified diff file to evaluate counterfactually over a scratch copy
  -paths string
    	comma-separated repo-relative paths the intended change touches
  -symbols string
    	comma-separated exact fact names the intended change touches

Examples:
  # Which constraints govern a change to this file, and its blast radius
  enola plan internal/auth/session.go

  # A whole directory as the target
  enola plan --paths=internal/auth

  # The verdicts a patch would produce, before it is applied
  enola plan --patch change.diff

See also: enola help constraints, enola help impact, enola help check
